---
description: User commenting standard — docstrings everywhere; inline only for complexity/API/why
globs: "**/*.py"
alwaysApply: false
---

Write clean, self-documenting code with highly descriptive variable and function names. Do not comment on obvious line-by-line executions. Instead, provide:

1. A clear Docstring at the top of every file explaining what the module does.
2. A Docstring for every function explaining its purpose, arguments, and return values.
3. Inline comments ONLY when explaining complex logic, API limitations, or why a specific approach was chosen.
